WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.413
One family cannot afford enough food or a safe home. Another family has food and a home, but far less than most families around them. Both are poor, in different ways.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:29.984
Absolute poverty means income is too low to pay for basic needs for survival: food, clean water and shelter. Relative poverty means a living standard below the typical standard in that society. The E U often uses income below sixty per cent of the median.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:39.968
Income inequality means income is spread unevenly, so there is a gap between groups. Here one household earns nine times as much as another.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:46.685
Why do governments act? To make sure basic needs are met, to raise living standards, and for fairness.

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:58.680
Step one, decide which idea is asked. Step two, give both parts of the definition. For inequality, say income is unevenly shared, and between which groups.

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:03.571
Step three, for a reason to act: name it, develop it, and use the case.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:21.661
Here is a real question from January 2023. The Scottish Government is giving thirty-seven point two million pounds to low-income households to tackle poverty and inequality. Explain one reason why it wants to reduce them. Three marks.

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:30.091
Pick one reason: to make sure basic needs are met. Low-income households may not afford food, heating or a safe home.

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:45.144
Apply it. The thirty-seven point two million pounds helps these families pay for essentials, so fewer people in Scotland live in poverty. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:54.237
A common mistake is swapping the two types. Can't meet basic needs is absolute. Below the typical standard is relative.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:02:00.069
Another is a vague definition. Being poor earns nothing. Say what it is compared with.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:18.693
Now you try. In Country K, the typical family earns nine hundred dollars a month. The Lee family earns three hundred and fifty. They can pay for food and rent, but little else. Absolute or relative poverty? Give one reason the government may help. Pause and decide.

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:30.915
They meet basic needs, so it is not absolute poverty. But sixty per cent of nine hundred is five hundred and forty, and they earn far less. This is relative poverty.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:43.768
One reason: to raise living standards. With so little left after rent and food, the Lees cannot afford things most families have. Help would lift their living standard closer to the typical level.

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:53.429
Remember: decide which idea, give both parts of the definition, and for reasons: name, develop, apply. Now try the practice questions.
